;; @ai-generated(guided)
(ns flutter-cljd.internal.collection.fuzz-red-test
  "Deterministic reproductions of the NEW signatures the step-6 fuzz campaign
   found (.claude/orchestrate/fuzz-findings.md). One deftest per signature class.

   Every test replays its shrunk op vector through `fuzz-test/run-ops!` — the same
   driver that found and shrank it, so the reproduction is exact: it applies the
   bounded post-jump boundary wait O5 needs and the anchor guard `check!` cannot do
   on its own. The rig header is REGENERATED from the seed rather than transcribed,
   so :animate?/:approx/:layout0/:cross0 can never drift out of sync with the
   generator.

   The remaining :known-red ones (real engine gaps) are excluded from the default run; two
   (NEW-6, NEW-8) were reclassified in step 7 as oracle/fuzzer miscalibration and
   are kept GREEN here so the recalibration itself stays covered. NEW-4 lived in
   an uncommitted seed-cache! WIP (preserved as
   .claude/orchestrate/wip-seed-cache-reanchor.patch); its test stays green as a
   guard against an unguarded re-anchor GC reappearing.

     clojure -M:cljd test -- -x \"known-red || fuzz\"   # green baseline
     clojure -M:cljd test -- -t known-red              # the reds only

   Step 10's re-campaign (220 episodes over four profiles) added NEW-9..NEW-13.
   NEW-9 (FIXED, step 10b) 17 seeds across all four profiles reduce to three ops —
   a cache invalidator (count or cross change), a drag, then a morph. The
   invalidator OPENS a segment; the drag moves the viewport mid-segment, where
   viewAnchor was never resampled; the morph's capture then consumed a
   pre-segment anchor whose slot lies outside the capture window, so `segAnchor`
   resolved nil and the produced rebase was discarded. viewAnchor now samples
   the displayed frame every pass (mid-segment included), and segment-start!
   guarantees the absorption channel: an anchorless capture that produced a
   rebase absorbs it as a pure shift over the first placed slot. NEW-10..NEW-13 are
   the residuals of signatures steps 9b/9c closed in their primary form:
   the set-point preserves the consumed fraction exactly and then applies it to
   the neighbouring item (NEW-10); known-B's re-anchor holds the INDEX again once
   a far jump precedes the insert (NEW-11); a rotation advertises a scrollExtent
   below the content of the same frame (NEW-12); and a morph following a far jump
   still caches most of the dataset without the count-change adjacency NEW-7
   needed (NEW-13).

   Confirmed diagnoses (step 7; the fixes belong to steps 8-11):

   NEW-1 (FIXED, stage 4) `segAnchor` translated the anchor slot rigidly by
     (:to − :from), pinning the anchor's TOP EDGE to a fixed screen position
     rather than the viewport-top item; a morph that shrinks a partly
     scrolled-past anchor (grid 208 -> list 109) then slid the top into the next
     item. The set-point now lerps the anchor's extent too and preserves the
     consumed FRACTION (`tw/point-desired`).

   NEW-2 (FIXED, stage 8) the seam was reconciled on the MAIN axis only, and the
     frozen re-anchor aligned the prefix on where :place puts the HEAD. When the
     prefix ends with an OPEN run that alignment drops the prefix's last run onto
     the retained head's run (observed: 303 and 304 both at cross 0, one offset).
     `refine-seam` reports the cross mismatch and the layout's new `:run-start`
     hook gives the alignment that leaves the head's run free.

   NEW-3 (FIXED, stage 9) `leading-step-entry`'s advance was
     `max(ext, flow-end(after i) − head)`. Wrap's :anchor seeds an EMPTY run at
     `head` and :place drops i into that same run, so flow-end returned `head`,
     the advance collapsed to the cell's own extent and the run gap was lost. The
     back-off reads the layout's `:run-start` (run pitch) instead.

   NEW-4 threw inside a seed-cache! cross-layout re-anchor WIP whose leading
     collectGarbage could destroy EVERY attached child before a non-nullable
     `^r/RenderBox (.-firstChild rs)` cast. The WIP is reverted; any re-anchor GC
     must nil-check firstChild after collecting and skip a GC that would empty
     the window.

   NEW-5 + NEW-7 (FIXED, stage 5) SHARED ONE ROOT: `keyed-tween-layout`'s
     :first-index/:last-index mapped \"the frozen snapshot has no opinion at this
     offset\" to index 0. Viewport BELOW the snapshot (`to-top` mid-segment) ⇒
     last-index 0 with first-index still inside the snapshot, an INVERTED window
     whose two garbage walks counted the same children twice (NEW-5). Viewport
     ABOVE it (a far jump mid-segment) ⇒ first-index 0, so the band stayed pinned
     at the top for the whole segment while `pixels` moved 16 000 px; the next
     layout swap then re-flowed the entire gap in one pass (NEW-7). Both queries
     clamp to the source's own edge, `indexed-layout!` refuses an inverted window,
     and a segment whose validity `:domain` the viewport leaves settles in place
     so the resting far-jump seed takes over."
  (:require
   [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]
   ["package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart" :as ft]
   [flutter-cljd.internal.collection.fuzz-test :as fz]))

;; --- replay plumbing ---

(defn- profile-of
  "The campaign's seed->profile split (fuzz-test §campaign)."
  [^int seed]
  (cond (< seed 100) :full
        (< seed 200) :no-layout
        (< seed 300) :no-jump
        :else :churn))

(defn- header-for [^int seed]
  (nth (fz/gen-episode seed (profile-of seed) fz/fuzz-items fz/episode-len) 0))

(defn- run-seed!
  "Replays `ops` on a fresh rig built from seed `seed`'s header."
  [^ft/WidgetTester t ^int seed ops]
  (await (fz/run-ops! t (header-for seed) ops)))

(defn- fail-str [f]
  (str "\n  header:  " (pr-str (dissoc (:header f) :seed :profile))
       "\n  ops:     " (pr-str (:ops f))
       "\n  failed:  op " (:op-index f) " " (pr-str (:op f))
       " kind=" (:kind f) " oracles=" (pr-str (:oracles f))
       "\n  viol:    " (pr-str (vec (take 3 (:violations f))))
       "\n  anchor0: " (pr-str (:anchor-before f))
       "\n  offset:  " (pr-str (:offset f)) " limits: " (pr-str (:limits f))
       "\n  engine:  " (pr-str (:engine f))))

;; --- the reds ---

(deftest fuzz-morph-holds-anchor-without-jump
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 26
                            [[:settle]
                             [:drag 576.4958953857422]
                             [:layout :list]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-1 grid->list morph after a plain drag moved the "
                      "viewport-top item (no far jump involved):" (fail-str f)))))

(deftest fuzz-wrap-runs-stay-disjoint-after-back-drag
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 222
                            [[:drag 4606.196022033691]
                             [:fling -2428.6102771759033]
                             [:drag -522.4222183227539]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-2 wrap cells overlap at rest after a backward drag:"
                      (fail-str f)))))

(deftest fuzz-wrap-run-advance-keeps-the-run-gap
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 240
                            [[:drag 3357.876420021057]
                             [:layout :wrap]
                             [:settle]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-3 the run after a morph starts one run-spacing early:"
                      (fail-str f)))))

(deftest fuzz-null-render-box-cast-in-morph-after-remove
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 5
                            [[:fling 4392.159795761108]
                             [:drag 805.7088088989258]
                             [:drag 788.5633134841919]
                             [:fling 7113.964653015137]
                             [:remove 284]
                             [:fling-catch -4022.814464569092 78]
                             [:drag -474.3441581726074]
                             [:layout :wrap]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-4 layout threw `type 'Null' is not a subtype of type "
                      "'RenderBox'`:" (fail-str f)))))

(deftest fuzz-garbage-counts-stay-within-child-count
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 6
                            [[:drag 3345.6783771514893]
                             [:cross 400.0]
                             [:settle]
                             [:cross 640.0]
                             [:jump 26061.590909957886]
                             [:to-top]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-5 collectGarbage asked to drop more children than are "
                      "attached (sliver_multi_box_adaptor.dart):" (fail-str f)))))

(deftest fuzz-count-change-then-far-jump-stays-window-bounded
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 32
                            [[:remove 331]
                             [:jump 16256.178617477417]
                             [:layout :wrap]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "NEW-7 one pass materialized the whole dataset after a "
                      "mid-segment far jump:" (fail-str f)))))

;; known-B in its fuzz-campaign form (intra-drift, seed 10): the harness_test red
;; covers the key-moved form
(deftest fuzz-insert-above-window-holds-anchor
  :tags [:widget]
  :runner (ft/testWidgets [tester])
  (let [f (await (run-seed! tester 10
                            [[:drag -251.21960163116455]
                             [:jump 17847.88191318512]
                             [:drag -420.46699047088623]
                             [:fling 3703.7041187286377]
                             [:drag 352.2779846191406]
                             [:fling 4489.896488189697]
                             [:drag -253.9003086090088]
                             [:drag -672.1532535552979]
                             [:pump 3]
                             [:pump 2]
                             [:insert 2 900010]]))]
    (is (nil? f) (str "known-B an insert above the window slid the content under "
                      "the viewport top:" (fail-str f)))))

;; --- step-10 campaign-2 signatures ---

(deftest fuzz-capture-rebase-has-absorption-channel
  :tags [:widget]
